From bd36cbea1f228c2e40c543627c5b5bd1fc399876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Care <tcare@meta.com>
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2025 13:54:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add graphics detection to mac and --verbose logging flag

Summary:
Implement graphics detection on Mac and add verbose logging with --verbose flag. This also allows for a pause to attach a debugger to the child process after fork().

This process is used in Cuttlefish initialization to detect supported graphics hardware APIs and quirks to pass to the emulator.

Note: A production version of this change should improve the Metal extension detection.

Test Plan:
Make sure swiftshader libEGL and libGLES are on the PATH, as well as libVulkan and MoltenVK.

$ m gfxstream_graphics_detector

$ gfxstream_graphics_detector
